  "notes": "Supplied by Shlomi on 2026-10-08 as T1500.pdf. Bituach Leumi form BL/1500 (05.2026), printed 'עמוד 3 מתוך 6' = pageIndex 3 of the 7-page file: section 6 (details of workplaces in the last 24 months, a two-employer table) and section 7 (military/national service dates). Flat Word export, no AcroForm. Geometry read from the page's own primitives (pdf.js text positions, ruled cell interiors and tick combs measured on the 150 DPI render, checkbox ink, underscore ink lines) and checked with overlay.mjs; never from a detector. Conventions copied from btl-bl211-2015-page7 and health-page1: (1) an underscore run is a one-line (11pt) writing strip above the printed line, as long as the run; kind `date` for date blanks (period from/until, termination-reason dates, notice-payment dates), `text` otherwise (percent, kinship type, reason). (2) a day/month/year tick comb is ONE `date` target with 8 cells; the two total-period (סה\"כ) tick combs are `comb` with 4 cells. (3) a ruled table cell a person writes into is kind `text` and the whole white interior, with label 'column caption / row caption' (name, occupation and job cells use the employer column header; address cells use their sub-header). (4) the printed square (measured ink of the ❑ glyph, drop shadow included) is the checkbox target; yes/no pairs and the reason list are independent `checkbox` targets, label 'option / question'. The two employer columns (מעסיק אחרון on the right, מעסיק נוסף או קודם on the left) repeat every caption, so the column is recorded in each target's notes. Not annotated: the two crossed-out (X) cells in the left column of the occupation and job rows, the 'הערה חשובה' box, the closing 'לידיעתך' sentence row, the section badges and every pre-printed caption (including the printed % sign and the חודשים/שנים captions under the total combs). Judgement calls: the 'הסיבה' blank under the התפטרות line is labelled 'הסיבה / התפטרות'; the right total comb's captions are split oddly in print (חוד / ים / שנים) and it is annotated as a 4-cell comb like its left twin. Checkbox bounds are the printed square without the shadow (FORM-31 convention).",
